// expect-note: NITPICK-MACRO-009
// expect-note-at: 61:72
//
// THE ROUND BOUND, AND WHO IS STANDING AT IT (D-057; DEF-173, 1.6.1e step 3 -- the
// library listener's mc0251).
//
// A cycle is refused at the declarations (`cycle_uninvoked.npk`), so what reaches
// the bound is a chain that is FINITE AND TOO LONG: thirty-three distinct macros,
// each emitting one function and invoking the next. Each round expands one level;
// after the thirty-second, `#link33()` is still standing where `link32`'s body
// wrote it.
//
// THE REFUSAL POINTS AT THAT INVOCATION AND NAMES ITS MACRO. It used to be reported
// "at the module" -- module 0, so `prelude.npk:17:1`, a file the reader did not
// write -- in a sentence that named nothing. The driver takes one more walk that
// instantiates nothing (the probe) and reports the first invocation it meets; the
// note says which invocation expanded the body that line is in.
//
// A CHAIN OF EXACTLY THIRTY-TWO SETTLES (tests/backend/programs/macro_chain_bound.npk):
// the bound is on rounds that still have something to expand, and the probe finds
// nothing standing after the thirty-second. Before this step that chain was
// refused too, with nothing left to refuse.
//
// GENERATED: `macro:linkK = () { func:rungK = int32() never fails { pass Ki32; };
// #link(K+1)(); };` for K in 1..32, a last `link33` that only emits, then
// `#link1();`. Regenerate it if `EXPAND_ROUNDS` moves.
mod:round_bound;

